WEBVTT

00:00:46.878 --> 00:00:49.121
Come on, let's say good
night to your brother.

00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:58.153
'Night Sam. Good night, love.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.154
Hey! Dean.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.503
Daddy! Hey! Buddy.

00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:06.336
What do you think? Sam is ready
to touch around football yet?

00:01:06.336 --> 00:01:08.200
No, daddy. No?

00:01:08.247 --> 00:01:09.931
You got him? I got him.

00:01:12.412 --> 00:01:14.126
Sweet dreams, Sammy.

00:01:45.456 --> 00:01:46.482
John?

00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:10.176
John, is he hungry?

00:02:12.314 --> 00:02:13.134
Okay.

00:02:54.719 --> 00:02:56.506
Sammy!

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:04.734
Mary!

00:03:05.882 --> 00:03:06.702
Mary!

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:12.245
Mary!

00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:21.214
Hey, Sammy.

00:03:22.948 --> 00:03:24.061
Okay?

00:03:41.595 --> 00:03:42.459
Mary!

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.129
Daddy!

00:03:57.222 --> 00:03:58.886
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:00.300
Don't look back!

00:04:00.486 --> 00:04:01.702
Now, Dean! Go!

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.518
It's okay, Sam.

00:04:29.786 --> 00:04:31.834
I got it. I got it.

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:36.436
Here.

00:04:52.539 --> 00:04:54.576
Stay back. You have to stay back.

00:05:14.456 --> 00:05:14.886
Sam!

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:17.155
Get a move on, would ya?

00:05:17.156 --> 00:05:19.261
We were supposed to be
there like 15 minutes ago.

00:05:20.282 --> 00:05:22.041
Sam, you coming or what?

00:05:22.633 --> 00:05:26.322
Do I have to? Yes. It'll be fun.

00:05:27.306 --> 00:05:29.051
And where's your costume?

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.059
You know how I feel about Halloween.

00:05:40.515 --> 00:05:43.376
So here's to Sam and his
awesome LSAT* victory.

00:05:43.483 --> 00:05:44.956
All right, all right.
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:44.957 --> 00:05:47.568
Yeah, he acts all humble,
but he scored a 174.

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:51.073
Is that good? Scary good.

00:05:51.115 --> 00:05:53.441
See, there you go. You are
a first-Round draft pick.

00:05:53.956 --> 00:05:55.812
You can go to any law school you want.

00:05:55.813 --> 00:05:58.082
Actually, I got an
interview here monday.

00:05:58.551 --> 00:06:01.706
If it goes okay, I think I got
a shot at a full ride next year.

00:06:01.747 --> 00:06:03.636
Hey, it's gonna go great.

00:06:05.048 --> 00:06:05.773
It better.

00:06:05.805 --> 00:06:08.216
How does it feel to be the
golden boy in your family?

00:06:08.222 --> 00:06:09.281
They don't know.

00:06:09.314 --> 00:06:12.111
No? I would be gloating. Why not?

00:06:12.161 --> 00:06:14.185
'Cause we're not exactly the Bradys

00:06:14.237 --> 00:06:16.588
I'm not exactly the
Huxtables. More shots?

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.381
No. No. No. No!

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:22.460
Seriously, I'm proud of you, and
you're gonna knock them dead on monday.

00:06:22.461 --> 00:06:23.882
You're gonna get that full ride.

00:06:24.245 --> 00:06:25.249
I know it.

00:06:26.086 --> 00:06:27.472
What would I do without you?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.968
Crash and burn.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.957
Whoa! Easy, tiger.

00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:34.383
Dean?

00:07:36.008 --> 00:07:37.471
You scared the crap out of me.

00:07:37.471 --> 00:07:38.921
That's cause you're out of practice.

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.289
Or not.

00:07:42.801 --> 00:07:43.941
Get off of me.

00:07:44.206 --> 00:07:45.975
Dean, what the hell are you doing here?

00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:48.182
I was looking for a beer.

00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:50.536
What the hell are you doing here?

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.341
Ok, all right, we got to talk.

00:07:53.386 --> 00:07:55.900
The phone? If I'd called
would you picked up?

00:07:56.426 --> 00:07:57.263
Sam?

00:07:58.601 --> 00:08:00.667
Jess, hey.

00:08:01.994 --> 00:08:04.002
Dean, this is my girlfriend, Jessica.

00:08:04.726 --> 00:08:06.567
Wait. Your brother Dean?

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:07.858
I love the Smurfs.

00:08:08.428 --> 00:08:12.173
You know, I got to tell you. You are
completely out of my brother's league.

00:08:12.279 --> 00:08:13.732
Just let me put something on.

00:08:13.779 --> 00:08:17.587
No, no. No, I wouldn't
dream of it, seriously.

00:08:18.623 --> 00:08:21.746
Anyway, I got to borrow your boyfriend here,
talk about some private family business, but

00:08:21.747 --> 00:08:22.938
Nice meeting you.

00:08:24.571 --> 00:08:25.549
No.

00:08:27.485 --> 00:08:29.586
No, whatever you want to say,
you can say it in front of her.

00:08:30.187 --> 00:08:31.190
Okay.

00:08:32.738 --> 00:08:34.723
Dad hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:35.692 --> 00:08:39.986
So? He's working overtime on a "Miller Time"
shift. He'll stumble back in sooner or later.

00:08:41.002 --> 00:08:43.520
Dad's on a hunting trip,

00:08:43.521 --> 00:08:45.942
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:50.874 --> 00:08:52.034
Jess, excuse us.

00:08:53.375 --> 00:08:55.642
We have to go outside.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:09:00.555
I mean, come on, you can't just break in the middle
of the night and expect me to hit the road with you.

00:09:00.556 --> 00:09:02.641
You're not hearing me,
Sammy. Dad's missing.

00:09:02.656 --> 00:09:04.465
I need you to help me find him.

00:09:04.253 --> 00:09:07.584
You remember the poltergeist in
Amherst, or the devil's gates in Clifton?

00:09:07.656 --> 00:09:10.997
He was missing then, too. He's
always missing, and he's always fine.

00:09:10.998 --> 00:09:13.359
Not for this long. Now, are
you gonna come with me or not?

00:09:13.676 --> 00:09:14.649
I'm not.

00:09:15.039 --> 00:09:15.756
Why not?

00:09:15.804 --> 00:09:18.106
I swore I was done hunting. For good.

00:09:18.361 --> 00:09:21.118
Come on, it wasn't easy,
but it wasn't that bad. Yeah?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.935
When I told dad I was scared of the
thing in my closet, he gave me a .45.

00:09:24.967 --> 00:09:26.067
What was he supposed to do?

00:09:26.101 --> 00:09:28.030
I was 9 years old.

00:09:28.759 --> 00:09:31.030
He was supposed to say:
"Don't be afraid of the dark."

00:09:31.088 --> 00:09:32.678
"Don't be afraid of the
dark"? Are you kidding me?

00:09:32.679 --> 00:09:34.836
Of course, you should be afraid.
You know what's out there.

00:09:34.877 --> 00:09:37.533
Yeah I know but still... The way
we grew up after mom was killed

00:09:37.546 --> 00:09:40.096
And dad's obsession to find
the thing that killed her.

00:09:40.141 --> 00:09:42.579
But we still haven't
found the damn thing.

00:09:42.709 --> 00:09:44.255
So we kill everything we can find.

00:09:44.387 --> 00:09:46.689
Save a lot of people doing it, too.

00:09:49.273 --> 00:09:51.026
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:56.779
The weapon training and
melting the silver into bullets?

00:09:56.856 --> 00:09:59.408
Man, Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:09:59.434 --> 00:10:00.475
So, what are you gonna do?

00:10:00.675 --> 00:10:03.419
Are you just gonna live
some normal, apple-Pie life?

00:10:03.036 --> 00:10:04.031
Is that it?

00:10:04.168 --> 00:10:06.487
No, not normal. Safe.

00:10:07.015 --> 00:10:08.772
And that's why you ran away.

00:10:12.182 --> 00:10:13.683
I was just going to college.

00:10:13.684 --> 00:10:16.969
It was dad who said if I was
gonna go, I should stay gone.

00:10:18.492 --> 00:10:19.551
And that's what I'm doing.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:23.513
Dad's in real trouble right now if
he's not dead already. I can feel it.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:27.846
I can't do this alone.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.465
Yes, you can.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.591
Yeah. Well, I don't want to.

00:10:41.037 --> 00:10:42.440
What was he hunting?

00:10:48.343 --> 00:10:51.548
All right. Let's see. Where
the hell did I put that thing?

00:10:51.614 --> 00:10:53.590
So when dad left, why
didn't you go with him?

00:10:53.823 --> 00:10:57.353
I was working my own gig... This
voodoo thing down in New Orleans.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.383
Dad let you go on a
hunting trip by yourself?

00:11:00.935 --> 00:11:02.210
I'm 26, dude.

00:11:03.621 --> 00:11:05.350
All right, here we go.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.888
So dad was checking out this two-Lane
blacktop just outside of Jericho, California.

00:11:09.987 --> 00:11:11.391
About a month ago, this guy...

00:11:11.656 --> 00:11:14.801
They found his car, but he'd
vanished. Completely M.I.A.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:17.192
So maybe he was kidnapped.

00:11:17.231 --> 00:11:19.249
Yeah, well, here's another one in April,

00:11:19.393 --> 00:11:24.861
Another one in December '04, '03, '98,
'92... 10 of them over the past 20 years...

00:11:25.156 --> 00:11:27.934
All men, all same
5-Mile stretch of road.

00:11:30.016 --> 00:11:32.103
Started happening more and more, so

00:11:32.136 --> 00:11:33.634
Dad went to go dig around.

00:11:33.656 --> 00:11:35.410
That was about three weeks ago.

00:11:35.815 --> 00:11:38.206
I hadn't heard from him
since, which is bad enough,

00:11:39.446 --> 00:11:41.524
And then I get this
voice mail yesterday.

00:11:42.067 --> 00:11:46.103
<i>Dean, something is starting to
happen. I think it's serious.</i>

00:11:46.191 --> 00:11:48.128
<i>I need to try to figure
out what's going on.</i>

00:11:51.817 --> 00:11:55.078
<i>Be very careful, Dean.
We're all in danger.</i>

00:11:55.746 --> 00:11:57.279
You know there's EVP on that?

00:11:57.377 --> 00:12:00.207
Not bad, Sammy. Kind of
like riding a bike, isn't it?

00:12:00.947 --> 00:12:04.010
All right. I slowed the message
down and ran it through a goldwave,

00:12:04.041 --> 00:12:05.778
Took out the hiss,
and this is what I got.

00:12:07.354 --> 00:12:10.919
<i>I can never go home.</i>

00:12:13.269 --> 00:12:14.865
Never go home.

00:12:20.642 --> 00:12:24.538
You know, in almost two years, I've never
bothered you, never asked you for a thing.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.221
All right, I'll go.

00:12:35.129 --> 00:12:36.615
I'll help you find him,

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.748
But I have to get back
first thing Monday.

00:12:39.108 --> 00:12:40.078
Just wait here.

00:12:40.396 --> 00:12:42.132
What's first thing monday?

00:12:43.607 --> 00:12:45.234
I've this...

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:47.742
I have an interview.

00:12:47.758 --> 00:12:49.567
What? A job interview? Skip it.

00:12:51.374 --> 00:12:55.667
It's a law-School interview, and
it's my whole future on a plate.

00:12:55.739 --> 00:12:56.663
Law school?

00:12:57.543 --> 00:12:59.201
So we got a deal or not?

00:13:03.461 --> 00:13:04.979
Wait, you're taking off?

00:13:05.259 --> 00:13:06.730
Is this about your dad? Is he all right?

00:13:06.871 --> 00:13:09.296
Yeah. You know, just
a little family drama.

00:13:09.769 --> 00:13:12.410
But your brother said he was
on some kind of hunting trip.

00:13:12.465 --> 00:13:15.104
Yeah, he's just deer
hunting up at the cabin,

00:13:15.256 --> 00:13:18.503
And he's probably got Jim,
Jack, and Jose along with him.

00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:20.165
We're just gonna go bring him back.

00:13:20.162 --> 00:13:21.257
What about the interview?

00:13:22.048 --> 00:13:23.206
I'll make the interview.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.750
This is only for a couple days.

00:13:24.856 --> 00:13:27.572
Sam, I mean, please.
Just stop for a second.

00:13:28.514 --> 00:13:29.594
You're sure you're okay?

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.570
I'm fine

00:13:32.356 --> 00:13:35.689
It's just... You want
even talk about your family

00:13:36.142 --> 00:13:39.148
And now you're taking off the middle of
the night to spend the week-End with them

00:13:39.367 --> 00:13:42.214
And with Monday coming up...
It's just not kind of your style.

00:13:42.259 --> 00:13:44.570
Hey, everything's gonna be okay.

00:13:45.375 --> 00:13:47.508
I would be back in time, I promise.

00:13:51.224 --> 00:13:52.747
At least tell me where you're going!

00:14:02.819 --> 00:14:04.571
Amy, I can't come over tonight.

00:14:05.543 --> 00:14:08.156
Because I got work in
the morning, that's why.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.020
Okay, I miss it, my
dad's gonna have my ass.

00:14:17.634 --> 00:14:19.370
Hey, uh, Amy, let me call you back.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.181
Car trouble or something?

00:14:39.365 --> 00:14:41.399
Take me home.

00:14:42.917 --> 00:14:44.168
Sure, get in.

00:15:00.389 --> 00:15:02.861
So where do you live?

00:15:05.834 --> 00:15:08.400
At the end of Breckenridge Road.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:12.817
You're coming from a
Halloween party or something?

00:15:16.576 --> 00:15:20.503
You know, um, a girl like you
really shouldn't be alone out here.

00:15:31.813 --> 00:15:33.550
I'm with you.

00:15:45.068 --> 00:15:47.133
Do you think I'm pretty?

00:15:51.936 --> 00:15:53.704
Will you come home with me?

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:56.770
Um...Hell, yeah.

00:16:16.487 --> 00:16:18.771
Come on. You don't live here.

00:16:20.272 --> 00:16:21.726
I can never go home

00:16:22.086 --> 00:16:26.138
What? What are you talking
about? Nobody lives here.

00:16:26.502 --> 00:16:28.239
Huh, where do you live?

00:16:35.331 --> 00:16:36.974
That's good.

00:16:37.835 --> 00:16:39.290
Joke's over, okay?

00:16:42.652 --> 00:16:44.201
You want me to leave?

00:17:04.028 --> 00:17:04.982
Hello?

00:17:12.421 --> 00:17:13.891
Hello?

00:18:14.627 --> 00:18:16.833
Hey. You want breakfast?

00:18:17.323 --> 00:18:18.434
No, thanks.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:23.315
So how'd you pay for that stuff? You
and dad still running credit-Card scams?

00:18:23.476 --> 00:18:26.762
Yeah, well, hunting ain't
exactly a pro-Ball career.

00:18:28.326 --> 00:18:30.896
Besides, all we do is apply. It's
not our fault they send us the cards.

00:18:30.927 --> 00:18:35.216
Yeah, and what names did you
write on the application this time?

00:18:35.284 --> 00:18:40.935
Uh... Bert Aframian and his son,
Hector. Scored two cards out of the deal.

00:18:41.029 --> 00:18:42.523
Sounds about right.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:45.643
I swear, man,you got to update
your cassette-Tape collection.

00:18:45.715 --> 00:18:46.435
Why?

00:18:46.576 --> 00:18:48.539
Well, for one... They're cassette tapes.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:49.540
And two...

00:18:49.541 --> 00:18:53.728
Black Sabbath, Motorhead, Metallica?

00:18:54.095 --> 00:18:56.787
It's the greatest hits of mullet rock.

00:18:57.027 --> 00:18:59.321
House rules, Sammy...
driver picks the music,

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.972
Shotgun shuts his cake hole.

00:19:01.739 --> 00:19:04.368
Yo Sammy is a chubby
12-Year-Old. It's...

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.154
Sorry, I can't hear you.
The music's too loud.

00:19:24.789 --> 00:19:26.001
Thank you.

00:19:27.211 --> 00:19:30.107
All right. So there's no one matching
dad at the hospital or morgue.

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:31.399
So that's something, I guess.

00:19:34.757 --> 00:19:35.789
Check it out.

00:19:59.488 --> 00:20:00.458
Let's go.

00:20:04.519 --> 00:20:06.272
Did you guys find anything?

00:20:06.303 --> 00:20:08.978
No! Nothing!

00:20:13.865 --> 00:20:17.062
No sign of struggle, no
footprints, no fingerprints...

00:20:17.063 --> 00:20:18.063
Spotless. It's almost too clean.

00:20:18.939 --> 00:20:20.564
So this kid, Troy...

00:20:20.565 --> 00:20:22.563
He's dating your daughter, isn't he? Ya.

00:20:22.564 --> 00:20:23.647
How's Amy doing?

00:20:23.757 --> 00:20:25.806
She's been putting up
missing posters downtown.

00:20:26.901 --> 00:20:29.639
You had another one like
this last month, didn't you?

00:20:30.828 --> 00:20:32.001
And who are you?

00:20:32.549 --> 00:20:33.988
Federal marshals.

00:20:35.526 --> 00:20:37.654
You two are a little young
for marshals, aren't you?

00:20:37.842 --> 00:20:39.500
Thanks, that's awfully kind of you.

00:20:40.068 --> 00:20:41.993
You did have another one
just like this, correct?

00:20:42.149 --> 00:20:42.900
Yeah, that's right,

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:45.419
About a mile up the road. There
have been others before that.

00:20:45.471 --> 00:20:48.178
So this victim... You knew him?

00:20:48.944 --> 00:20:50.931
A town like this,
everybody knows everybody.

00:20:50.994 --> 00:20:53.779
Any connection between the victims
besides that they're all men?

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.748
No. Not so far as we can tell.

00:20:56.108 --> 00:20:57.156
So what's the theory?

00:20:57.286 --> 00:20:58.609
Honestly, we don't know...

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.031
Serial murderer, kidnapping ring.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:05.140
Well, that is exactly the kind of crack
police work I'd expect out of you guys.

00:21:05.598 --> 00:21:07.585
Thank you for your time.

00:21:08.054 --> 00:21:09.822
Gentlemen.

00:21:18.313 --> 00:21:19.328
What was that for?

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.955
Why do you have to step on my foot? Why
do you have to talk to police like that?

00:21:22.165 --> 00:21:24.574
Come on. They don't really
know what's going on.

00:21:24.682 --> 00:21:25.842
We're all alone on this.

00:21:25.843 --> 00:21:28.931
If we're gonna find dad, we've got to
get to the bottom of this thing ourselves.

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.996
Can I help you boys?

00:21:33.508 --> 00:21:35.308
No, sir. We were just leaving.

00:21:35.309 --> 00:21:37.604
Agent Mulder, agent Scully.

00:21:45.994 --> 00:21:47.324
I'll bet you that's her.

00:21:47.622 --> 00:21:48.529
Yeah.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.221
You must be Amy. Yeah.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:55.574
Troy told us about you. We're his
uncles. I'm Dean. This is Sammy.

00:21:55.809 --> 00:21:57.170
He never mentioned you to me.

00:21:57.749 --> 00:21:58.969
Well, that's Troy, I guess.

00:21:59.016 --> 00:22:00.719
We're not around much.
We're up in Modesto.

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.630
So we're looking for him, too,
and we're kind of asking around.

00:22:04.835 --> 00:22:07.025
Hey, are you okay? Yeah.

00:22:07.265 --> 00:22:09.471
Do you mind if we ask
you a couple questions?

00:22:10.524 --> 00:22:13.210
I was on the phone with
Troy. He was driving home.

00:22:13.211 --> 00:22:18.064
He said he would call me
right back, and he never did.

00:22:18.065 --> 00:22:20.620
He didn't say anything
strange? Or out of the ordinary?

00:22:20.766 --> 00:22:23.613
No, nothing I can remember.

00:22:25.057 --> 00:22:26.403
I like your necklace.

00:22:29.145 --> 00:22:30.381
Troy gave it to me.

00:22:31.028 --> 00:22:34.955
Mostly to scare my parents...
You know, the devil stuff.

00:22:37.431 --> 00:22:39.650
Actually it means just the opposite.

00:22:39.661 --> 00:22:42.398
A pentagram is a
protection against evil.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.504
Really powerfull, I mean if
you believe in a kind of thing.

00:22:45.649 --> 00:22:47.996
Ok, thank you, Unsolved Mysteries.

00:22:48.246 --> 00:22:49.450
Here's the deal, ladies...

00:22:49.451 --> 00:22:52.954
The way Troy disappeared...
Something's not right.

00:22:52.955 --> 00:22:55.058
So if you've heard anything...

00:22:57.351 --> 00:22:58.259
What is it?

00:22:58.947 --> 00:22:59.877
Well, it's just...

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:02.906
I mean, with all these guys
going missing, people talk.

00:23:02.952 --> 00:23:04.141
What do they talk about?

00:23:07.916 --> 00:23:10.028
It's kind of this local legend.

00:23:10.294 --> 00:23:14.925
This one girl, she got murdered
out on Centennial like decades ago.

00:23:15.529 --> 00:23:18.173
Well, supposedly, she's still out there.

00:23:18.569 --> 00:23:21.959
She hitchhikes, and
whoever picks her up...

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:25.132
Well, they disappear forever.

00:23:42.232 --> 00:23:44.062
Let me try. I got it.

00:23:45.423 --> 00:23:46.268
Dude.

00:23:47.785 --> 00:23:49.944
You're such a control freak.

00:23:50.679 --> 00:23:53.667
So angry spirits are born out
of violent death, right? Yeah

00:23:54.043 --> 00:23:55.451
Maybe it's not murder.

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:09.673
This was 1981. Constance Welch, 24 years old,
jumps off Sylvania Bridge, drowns in the river.

00:24:09.704 --> 00:24:11.461
Does it say why she did it? Yeah.

00:24:11.852 --> 00:24:12.415
What?

00:24:13.151 --> 00:24:15.502
An hour before they
found her, she calls 911.

00:24:15.565 --> 00:24:18.716
Her two little kids are in the bathtub.
She leaves them alone for a minute,

00:24:18.717 --> 00:24:19.889
And when she comes back,

00:24:19.961 --> 00:24:21.213
They aren't breathing.

00:24:21.893 --> 00:24:22.910
Both died.

00:24:23.901 --> 00:24:26.488
"Our babies were gone, and
Constance just couldn't bear it,"

00:24:26.489 --> 00:24:27.489
Said husband, Joseph Welch.

00:24:29.867 --> 00:24:31.964
That bridge look familiar to you?

00:24:36.959 --> 00:24:39.963
So this is where Constance
took the swan dive.

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:42.111
So you think dad would have been here?

00:24:42.893 --> 00:24:45.615
Well, he's chasing the same
story, and we're chasing him.

00:24:47.028 --> 00:24:48.374
Okay, so now what?

00:24:49.359 --> 00:24:51.909
Now we keep digging till we
find him. It might take a while.

00:24:52.107 --> 00:24:55.721
Dean, I told you I've got
to get back by... Monday.

00:24:56.863 --> 00:24:58.631
Right. The interview.

00:24:58.678 --> 00:25:00.258
Yeah. Yeah, I forgot.

00:25:00.921 --> 00:25:02.767
You're really serious
about this, aren't you?

00:25:03.768 --> 00:25:05.974
You think you're just
gonna become some lawyer,

00:25:06.350 --> 00:25:07.601
Marry your girl?

00:25:07.664 --> 00:25:08.806
Maybe. Why not?

00:25:09.014 --> 00:25:12.394
Does Jessica know the truth about you?
Does she know about the things you've done?

00:25:12.597 --> 00:25:14.365
No, and she's not ever going to know.

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:16.602
Well, that's healthy.

00:25:16.904 --> 00:25:21.425
You can pretend all you want, Sammy, but sooner or
later you're gonna have to face up to who you really are.

00:25:21.852 --> 00:25:22.611
Who is that?

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:24.117
One of us. No!

00:25:24.246 --> 00:25:26.787
I'm not like you. This is
not going to be my life.

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:29.878
Well, you have a responsibility. To dad?

00:25:29.206 --> 00:25:30.911
And his crusade?

00:25:31.286 --> 00:25:34.337
If it weren't for pictures, I
wouldn't even know what mom looks like.

00:25:34.732 --> 00:25:36.109
What difference would it make?

00:25:36.359 --> 00:25:38.503
Even if we do find the
thing that killed her,

00:25:39.301 --> 00:25:42.086
Mom's gone, and she isn't coming back.

00:25:48.329 --> 00:25:50.675
Don't talk about her like that.

00:25:59.872 --> 00:26:00.795
Sam.

00:26:13.621 --> 00:26:15.420
Where'd she go? I don't know.

00:26:19.779 --> 00:26:23.424
What the...? Who's driving your car?

00:26:31.108 --> 00:26:33.955
Come on, Dean. Let's go! Go!

00:27:00.356 --> 00:27:01.216
Dean!

00:27:02.637 --> 00:27:03.310
Dean!

00:27:06.134 --> 00:27:06.979
What?!

00:27:10.745 --> 00:27:12.920
Hey, are you all right?

00:27:13.859 --> 00:27:15.032
I'm super.

00:27:20.740 --> 00:27:22.054
Car all right?

00:27:22.257 --> 00:27:24.854
Yeah, whatever she did to
it, it seems all right now.

00:27:25.089 --> 00:27:27.233
That Constance chick... What a bitch!

00:27:27.467 --> 00:27:30.236
Well, she doesn't want us
digging around, that's for sure.

00:27:32.197 --> 00:27:34.481
So where's the trail
go from here, genius?

00:27:39.973 --> 00:27:41.553
You smell like a toilet.

00:27:44.565 --> 00:27:45.785
One room, please.

00:27:49.649 --> 00:27:51.543
You guys having a reunion or something?

00:27:51.840 --> 00:27:52.513
What do you mean?

00:27:52.846 --> 00:27:57.273
That other guy, Bert Aframian. He came in
and bought out a room for the whole month.

00:28:27.939 --> 00:28:30.500
I don't think he's been here
for a couple days at least.

00:28:32.664 --> 00:28:35.323
Salt, cat's-Eye shells...

00:28:35.746 --> 00:28:39.506
He was worried, trying to
keep something from coming in.

00:28:42.525 --> 00:28:43.636
What do you got here?

00:28:44.104 --> 00:28:46.717
Centennial Highway victims.

00:28:48.266 --> 00:28:49.596
I don't get it.

00:28:50.159 --> 00:28:54.070
I mean, different men,
different jobs, age, ethnicities.

00:28:54.780 --> 00:28:56.548
There's always a connection, right?

00:28:57.377 --> 00:28:58.801
What do these guys have in common?

00:29:13.930 --> 00:29:15.260
Dad figured it out.

00:29:15.529 --> 00:29:16.781
What do you mean?

00:29:16.829 --> 00:29:18.898
He found the same article we did.

00:29:18.899 --> 00:29:22.313
Constance Welch. She's a woman in white.

00:29:25.288 --> 00:29:26.774
You sly dogs.

00:29:27.071 --> 00:29:30.435
All right, so if we're dealing with a woman in white,
dad would have found the corpse and destroyed it.

00:29:30.623 --> 00:29:32.219
She might have another weakness.

00:29:32.743 --> 00:29:35.270
No, dad would want to
make sure. He'd dig her up.

00:29:35.329 --> 00:29:36.693
Does it say where she's buried?

00:29:37.117 --> 00:29:38.916
No, not that I can tell.

00:29:39.433 --> 00:29:41.639
If I were dad, though,
I'd go ask her husband,

00:29:42.061 --> 00:29:43.313
If he's still alive.

00:29:49.882 --> 00:29:53.027
All right, why don't you see if you can
find an address? I'm gonna get cleaned up.

00:29:53.469 --> 00:29:58.366
Hey, Dean, what I said earlier
about mom and dad... I'm sorry.

00:29:59.195 --> 00:30:00.618
No chick-Flick moments.

00:30:01.797 --> 00:30:03.596
All right... jerk.

00:30:04.738 --> 00:30:05.614
Bitch.

00:30:22.936 --> 00:30:26.362
<i>Hey, it's me. It's about 10:20...</i>

00:30:26.878 --> 00:30:31.077
Hey, man. I'm starving. I'm gonna grab a little
something to eat at that diner down the street.

00:30:31.078 --> 00:30:32.386
You want anything?

00:30:32.693 --> 00:30:33.262
No.

00:30:33.262 --> 00:30:34.559
Aframian's buying.

00:30:52.055 --> 00:30:54.590
<i>So come home soon, okay? I love you.</i>

00:30:57.453 --> 00:30:57.985
What?

00:30:58.224 --> 00:30:59.554
Dude, five-O. Take off.

00:31:00.023 --> 00:31:01.040
What about you?

00:31:01.306 --> 00:31:03.903
Uh, they kind of
spotted me. Go find dad.

00:31:05.875 --> 00:31:07.064
Problem, officers?

00:31:07.236 --> 00:31:08.487
Where's your partner?

00:31:08.736 --> 00:31:10.786
Partner? What? What partner?

00:31:18.227 --> 00:31:21.825
So fake U.S. Marshal, fake credit cards.

00:31:22.091 --> 00:31:23.546
You got anything that's real?

00:31:24.094 --> 00:31:25.001
My boobs.

00:31:26.933 --> 00:31:29.076
You have the right to remain silent.

00:31:31.382 --> 00:31:33.572
So you want to give us your real name?

00:31:33.922 --> 00:31:37.176
I told you. It's Nugent, Ted Nugent.

00:31:39.366 --> 00:31:42.370
I'm not sure you realize just
how much trouble you're in here.

00:31:42.371 --> 00:31:46.724
We're talking, like, misdemeanor kind of
trouble or "squeal like a pig" trouble?

00:31:47.084 --> 00:31:49.838
You got the faces of 10 missing
persons taped to your wall,

00:31:50.250 --> 00:31:53.160
Along with a whole lot
of satanic mumbo jumbo.

00:31:53.535 --> 00:31:55.475
Boy, you are officially a suspect.

00:31:55.637 --> 00:31:59.611
That makes sense 'cause when the
first one went missing in '82, I was 3.

00:32:00.158 --> 00:32:03.068
I know you got partners.
One of them's an older guy.

00:32:03.851 --> 00:32:05.822
Maybe he started the whole thing.

00:32:07.501 --> 00:32:09.707
So tell me, Dean...

00:32:12.106 --> 00:32:13.029
Is this his?

00:32:20.606 --> 00:32:22.108
I thought that might be your name.

00:32:23.735 --> 00:32:25.281
See, I leafed through this,

00:32:25.295 --> 00:32:28.872
What little I could make out. I
mean, it's nine kinds of crazy,

00:32:30.472 --> 00:32:32.193
But I found this, too.

00:32:33.269 --> 00:32:38.964
Now, you're staying right here till you
tell me exactly what the hell that means.

00:32:51.257 --> 00:32:54.386
Hi, uh, are you Joseph Welch? Yeah.

00:32:55.272 --> 00:32:57.013
Yeah, he was older, but that's him.

00:32:57.095 --> 00:33:00.462
He came by three or four days
ago, said he was a reporter.

00:33:00.821 --> 00:33:03.293
That's right. We're
working on a story together.

00:33:04.542 --> 00:33:08.563
Well, I don't know what the hell kind of story
you're working on... the questions he asked me.

00:33:08.641 --> 00:33:10.471
About your late wife, Constance.

00:33:11.441 --> 00:33:13.178
He asked me where she was buried.

00:33:14.028 --> 00:33:15.639
And where is that again?

00:33:16.249 --> 00:33:17.767
What? I got to go through these twice?

00:33:18.064 --> 00:33:20.409
It's fact checking, if you don't mind.

00:33:23.037 --> 00:33:26.448
In a plot behind my old
place over on Breckenridge.

00:33:27.063 --> 00:33:28.612
Why did you move?

00:33:30.035 --> 00:33:33.477
I'm not gonna live in the
house where my children died.

00:33:36.193 --> 00:33:38.274
Mr. Welch, did you ever marry again?

00:33:38.399 --> 00:33:42.013
No way. Constance... She
was the love of my life,

00:33:43.607 --> 00:33:45.438
Prettiest woman I ever known.

00:33:45.657 --> 00:33:47.096
So you had a happy marriage?

00:33:50.613 --> 00:33:51.411
Definitely.

00:33:54.493 --> 00:33:57.215
Well, that should do
it. Thanks for your time.

00:34:07.801 --> 00:34:10.639
Mr. Welch, you ever
hear of a woman in white?

00:34:10.821 --> 00:34:11.556
A what?

00:34:12.025 --> 00:34:15.170
A woman in white or
sometimes a weeping woman.

00:34:16.207 --> 00:34:17.193
It's a ghost story.

00:34:17.416 --> 00:34:20.718
Well, it's more of a phenomenon, really.

00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:24.494
They're spirits. They've been
sighted for hundreds of years,

00:34:24.854 --> 00:34:29.068
Dozens of places in Hawaii and
Mexico, lately in Arizona, Indiana.

00:34:29.109 --> 00:34:30.987
All these are different
women, you understand,

00:34:31.273 --> 00:34:33.150
But all share the same story.

00:34:34.089 --> 00:34:37.254
Boy, I don't care much for nonsense.

00:34:37.411 --> 00:34:38.772
You see, when they were alive,

00:34:39.215 --> 00:34:41.249
Their husbands were unfaithful to them,

00:34:42.156 --> 00:34:43.236
And these women,

00:34:43.596 --> 00:34:46.662
Basically suffering from temporary
insanity, murdered their children.

00:34:48.332 --> 00:34:51.680
Then, once they realized what they
had done, they took their own lives.

00:34:51.977 --> 00:34:53.729
So now their spirits are cursed,

00:34:54.058 --> 00:34:56.076
Walking back roads, waterways,

00:34:56.410 --> 00:34:59.476
And if they find an
unfaithful man, they kill him,

00:34:59.914 --> 00:35:01.651
And that man is never seen again.

00:35:03.294 --> 00:35:04.764
You think...

00:35:05.921 --> 00:35:09.614
You think that has something
to do with Constance,

00:35:10.240 --> 00:35:11.413
You smart ass?

00:35:12.007 --> 00:35:13.149
You tell me.

00:35:16.574 --> 00:35:21.048
I mean, maybe... Maybe
I made some mistakes,

00:35:21.627 --> 00:35:23.301
But no matter what I did,

00:35:23.990 --> 00:35:26.728
Constance never would have
killed her own children.

00:35:28.156 --> 00:35:30.253
Now, you get the hell out of here,

00:35:30.691 --> 00:35:32.302
And you don't come back.

00:35:47.779 --> 00:35:49.750
I don't know how many
times I got to tell you.

00:35:49.969 --> 00:35:51.581
It's my high-School locker combo.

00:35:52.008 --> 00:35:53.698
Are we gonna do this all night long?

00:35:53.776 --> 00:35:56.858
We just got a 911. Shots
fired over at Whiteford Road.

00:35:58.814 --> 00:36:00.331
Do you have to go to the bathroom?

00:36:00.962 --> 00:36:01.604
No.

00:36:01.932 --> 00:36:02.996
Good.

00:36:52.987 --> 00:36:56.179
Fake 911 phone call, Sammy?
That's pretty illegal.

00:36:56.460 --> 00:36:57.227
You're welcome.

00:36:57.321 --> 00:36:58.604
Listen, we got to talk

00:36:58.697 --> 00:37:01.440
Tell me about it. So the
husband was unfaithful.

00:37:01.534 --> 00:37:03.223
We are dealing with a woman in white.

00:37:03.301 --> 00:37:05.874
She's buried behind her old house.

00:37:05.895 --> 00:37:07.095
Sammy, would you shut up for a second?

00:37:07.139 --> 00:37:09.267
I can't figure out why he
hasn't destroyed the corpse yet.

00:37:09.470 --> 00:37:11.911
That's what I'm trying
to tell you. He's gone.

00:37:12.307 --> 00:37:13.386
Dad left Jericho.

00:37:13.433 --> 00:37:15.279
What? How do you know?

00:37:16.093 --> 00:37:16.906
I've got his journal.

00:37:17.094 --> 00:37:18.705
He doesn't go anywhere
without that thing.

00:37:18.898 --> 00:37:19.993
Well, he did this time.

00:37:20.056 --> 00:37:20.807
What's it say?

00:37:20.838 --> 00:37:23.936
Same old ex-Marine crap when he
wants to let us know where he's going.

00:37:23.999 --> 00:37:24.807
Coordinates.

00:37:24.810 --> 00:37:25.810
Where to?

00:37:25.810 --> 00:37:26.977
I'm not sure yet.

00:37:27.002 --> 00:37:31.100
I don't understand. I mean,
what can be so important

00:37:31.101 --> 00:37:32.101
That he just gets out
in the middle of the job?

00:37:31.717 --> 00:37:33.484
Dean, what the hell is going on?

00:37:36.956 --> 00:37:38.348
Sam, Sam!

00:37:44.757 --> 00:37:46.165
Take me home.

00:37:54.135 --> 00:37:56.341
Take me home.

00:37:58.176 --> 00:37:58.958
No.

00:38:39.811 --> 00:38:41.062
Don't do this.

00:38:43.649 --> 00:38:45.260
I can never go home.

00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:50.130
You're scared to go home.

00:38:57.144 --> 00:38:58.224
Hold me.

00:38:59.303 --> 00:39:01.760
I'm so cold.

00:39:02.171 --> 00:39:06.160
You can't kill me. I'm not unfaithful.

00:39:06.395 --> 00:39:08.194
I've never been.

00:39:09.409 --> 00:39:10.473
You will be.

00:39:55.088 --> 00:39:56.434
I'm taking you home.

00:39:58.905 --> 00:39:59.468
Sam!

00:40:10.554 --> 00:40:12.322
Sam! Here!

00:40:12.369 --> 00:40:13.511
You okay?

00:40:14.199 --> 00:40:15.075
I think.

00:40:15.670 --> 00:40:17.798
Can you move? Yeah. Help me.

00:41:19.177 --> 00:41:21.351
You've come home to us, mommy.

00:41:59.460 --> 00:42:01.431
So this is where she drowned her kids.

00:42:03.105 --> 00:42:04.576
That's why she could never go home.

00:42:06.367 --> 00:42:08.119
She was too scared to face them.

00:42:09.379 --> 00:42:10.959
You found her weak spot.

00:42:11.428 --> 00:42:12.711
Nice work, Sammy.

00:42:15.297 --> 00:42:17.441
I wish I could say the same for you.

00:42:17.566 --> 00:42:19.859
What were you thinking shooting
Casper in the face, you freak?

00:42:19.964 --> 00:42:22.468
Hey, saved your ass.

00:42:23.359 --> 00:42:26.379
I'll tell you another thing.
If you screwed up my car,

00:42:27.942 --> 00:42:29.162
I'll kill you.

00:42:41.735 --> 00:42:44.973
Okay, here's where dad went. It's
called Blackbottle Ridge, Colorado.

00:42:46.209 --> 00:42:47.977
Sounds charming. How far?

00:42:48.191 --> 00:42:50.052
About 600 miles.

00:42:50.756 --> 00:42:53.087
If we shag ass, we
can make it by morning.

00:42:54.976 --> 00:42:56.540
Dean, um...

00:42:59.122 --> 00:43:00.154
You're not going.

00:43:00.295 --> 00:43:02.720
The interview's in 10
hours. I got to be there.

00:43:07.536 --> 00:43:11.651
Yeah. Yeah, whatever.
I'll take you home.

00:43:32.244 --> 00:43:33.731
You'll call me if you find him?

00:43:36.739 --> 00:43:38.476
Maybe I can meet up with you later, huh?

00:43:38.773 --> 00:43:39.633
Yeah, all right.

00:43:43.635 --> 00:43:44.417
Sam.

00:43:48.485 --> 00:43:50.237
You know, we made a hell
of a team back there.

00:43:51.479 --> 00:43:52.073
Yeah.

00:44:11.328 --> 00:44:12.204
Jess!

00:44:14.082 --> 00:44:15.208
You home!?

00:44:57.347 --> 00:44:58.286
No!

00:45:01.232 --> 00:45:02.202
Sam!

00:45:02.233 --> 00:45:03.000
Jess!

00:45:04.752 --> 00:45:06.270
Sam! Sam!

00:45:07.521 --> 00:45:09.320
No! No!

00:45:10.237 --> 00:45:12.991
Jess! Jess! No!

00:45:58.992 --> 00:46:00.713
We got work to do.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
